# Step 21, the editor: its rules broken one at a time, with the tests that
# must fail. Written with the code.
#
# One rule lives in Windows-only code, which this command cannot break where
# it runs: the console handler answers Ctrl+C as handled while the interrupt
# guard lives (`crates/cortex-term/src/sys/windows.rs`). The Windows run of
# `external::sys_ctrl_c_ends_the_editor_and_not_the_application` is what
# checks it.

